{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call_ZApfLLjL7MxRdQUeBvHP9EvQ\nfc_013758e78cde0696016aef568ece5c87d19eecdb28dbaff541","tool_call":{"taskToolCall":{"args":{"description":"Trace HEAD and refs","prompt":"Other explorers are investigating different slices of the same subsystem in parallel. Don't try to cover everything. Focus on your assigned angle and go deep. Work strictly read-only. Do not modify files, refs, index, objects, or working tree.\n\nRepository: /private/var/folders/11/m_kwnqr97632l_cjt0mhytvh0000gn/T/pstack-corpus-ur5cbW/20-PROMPT-HOW-READONLY-EXPLORERS-r1/cursor/work\n\n## Question\n> How does this repository's git storage work end to end? Cover how HEAD, the refs, the index, and the object store fit together to produce README.md in the working tree.\n\n## Your Exploration Angle\nTrace HEAD and reference resolution in this concrete repository. Inspect .git/HEAD, loose and packed refs, relevant logs/config where useful, and use read-only Git plumbing commands. Explain exactly how Git reaches the current commit and where branch identity versus commit identity is stored. Connect the resolved commit to the next storage layer, but leave detailed object and index analysis to other explorers.\n\n## Output\n\n### Components Found\nThe key types, services, classes, and abstractions. For each: name, file path, and a one-sentence description of what it does.\n\n### Flow\nThe execution flow step by step. For each step: what command/storage lookup runs, what file it's in, what it does, what it calls or resolves next. Include the data that flows between steps.\n\n### Files Read\nEvery file you read during exploration, so the explainer can reference them.\n\n### Boundaries\nWhere this subsystem connects to other parts of the repository. The inputs and outputs.\n\n### Non-Obvious Things\nAnything surprising, historically motivated, or easy to get wrong. Things that look like they should work one way but work another.\n\n### Open Questions\nAnything you couldn't fully trace or understand. Be honest about gaps.","subagentType":{"unspecified":{}},"model":"grok-4.7-high-fast","agentId":"b728d7f9-10be-4112-9e9f-137e9c838e52","attachments":[],"mode":"TASK_MODE_UNSPECIFIED","respondingToMessageIds":[],"environment":"SUBAGENT_EXECUTION_ENVIRONMENT_UNSPECIFIED","machine":{"sameMachine":{}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call_ZApfLLjL7MxRdQUeBvHP9EvQ\nfc_013758e78cde0696016aef568ece5c87d19eecdb28dbaff541","startedAtMs":"1794070158941"},"model_call_id":"d7f868af-c671-4b93-a9b4-3c821b6d8816-3-n7p8","session_id":"a41303d3-a890-432a-b0aa-6668a1db8c6e","timestamp_ms":1794070158981}
